{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778782495,"nonce":"7goJgEp9NCjO47Le/tE4TOnUikI=","title":"Lazy-import IPython.display in plot_utils.py so web backend boots without notebook deps","message":"Follow-up to issue 681d14f (ipywidgets lazy-import, merged in commit 2b89a43).\n\nAfter that fix, the next blocker on the web boot path is the unconditional `from IPython.display import HTML, display` at plot_utils.py:19. The web app still cannot start in a venv without the notebook extra installed.\n\nAudit:\n- `IPython.display.HTML` and `display` are referenced at two sites in plot_utils.py:\n  1. `plotly_vscode_latex_fix()` (line 198-203) - runs only inside VS Code notebooks (gated on VSCODE_PID env var)\n  2. `PlotlyFigureWidget.show()` (line 335) - the same notebook-only widget class whose other deps were just made lazy\n- Both are notebook-display-only paths.\n- IPython is also imported in `feedbax/setup_utils.py:21` and `feedbax/_treescope.py:98`, but `_treescope` already does it lazily inside a function, and `setup_utils` is not on the web boot path (it is imported lazily inside `feedbax/web/api/analysis.py:71`).\n- IPython is not declared anywhere in pyproject.toml as a direct dep - it comes transitively via the `notebook` extra (ipywidgets / notebook pull it in).\n\nFix:\n1. Remove the top-level `from IPython.display import HTML, display` from `feedbax/plot_utils.py`.\n2. Move it inside the two functions that use it: `plotly_vscode_latex_fix()` and `PlotlyFigureWidget.show()`. (Or whichever lazy-import site is cleanest - one import inside each function is fine; one in PlotlyFigureWidget.create_widgets covering both `widgets` and `HTML/display` is also acceptable.)\n\nTest protocol (stricter than previous PR to catch cascading misses):\n- Verify in a venv that has NEITHER `ipywidgets` NOR `IPython` installed.\n- `develop` worktree venv at `worktrees/develop/.venv` is the gold standard - it currently lacks both.\n- After fix, `uv run python -c \"from feedbax.web.app import app; print(type(app).__name__)\"` must succeed in that env, AND `uvicorn feedbax.web.app:app --port 8000` must boot cleanly.","files":null}]}